  { title: 'You set rates per license, per 1,000 pages.', text: `Summarization covers "a summary, grounding, or citation with a single use license". Full Display lets a buyer "display the complete text of an article once". Custom is for a partner you have a deal with. Rates can differ by bot, page, keyword, time and directory (${a(T.settingRates, 'Setting rates')}).` },
  { title: 'Buyers find you through TollBit and buy a pass for one URL.', text: `One API key searches TollBit's index, which covers sites "across the web" and flags TollBit's own. It shows each URL's licenses and prices (${a(T.licensedSearch, 'Licensed search')}, ${a(T.rates, 'Rates')}).` },
  { title: 'The pass is short-lived.', text: `TollBit calls it a token: "Tokens expire 5 minutes after issuance." Each works once and names the buyer's agent, the license type and the most the buyer will pay (${a(T.tokens, 'Tokens')}).` },
  { title: 'TollBit delivers the page.', text: `With a pass, TollBit fetches your page from your site, strips what you exclude, and returns Markdown or HTML (${a(T.security, 'Security')}; ${a(T.overview, 'Platform overview')}, §3.5).` },
  { title: 'Billing waits for delivery.', text: `Nobody is billed "until the token is actually accepted and a 200 OK response is delivered" (${a(T.overview, 'Platform overview')}, §5.1).` },
  { title: 'Your rate is your net.', text: `The buyer pays your rate plus "a small transaction fee on top of the rates you set" (${a(T.settingRates, 'Setting rates')}). TollBit doesn't publish the fee's size. You're paid through Stripe early each month, in US dollars (${a(T.overview, 'Platform overview')}, §1.4; ${a(T.tokens, 'Tokens')}).` },
];

