  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" id="together" label="Running both" title="Both on one site today. TollBit's rates behind a Broker, as a design." asideWidth="400px" asideAlign="start">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <h3 class="sub-h">On one site <StatusTag status="live" /></h3>
      <p class="prose" set:html={`TollBit's docs ask "Can I use another AI marketplace like TollBit in parallel?" The answer: "Yes, this is dependent on how you set up your log exports and bot redirect policies" (${a(T.architecture, 'Platform architecture')}). Order your CDN rules like this.`} />
      <StepList items={BOTH_STEPS} />
      <p class="prose" set:html={`On Cloudflare Enterprise, "Snippets execute earlier in Cloudflare's traffic sequence than Worker routes", so TollBit's rule runs first. On other plans "CloudFlare only runs one Worker per route", so your engineers combine TollBit's rule and FORA's edge function in one Worker (${a(T.cloudflare, 'Cloudflare')}; ${a('/components/edge-function/composition/', 'Composition')}).`} />
      <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.edgeFunction} />
      <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.signedLink} />
      <h3 class="sub-h">Behind a FORA Broker <StatusTag status="design" /></h3>
      <p class="prose" set:html={`A Broker would call TollBit's API with each agent's own TollBit account, never one of its own, as TollBit lets a platform act for a buyer (${a(T.overview, 'Platform overview')}, §4.3). An Exchange would sign each TollBit rate as a FORA offer, so the agent sees both offers and decides. How a Broker orders offers is on the ${a('/resources/content-marketplaces/#broker-order', 'hub')}.`} />
      <h3 class="sub-h">Doesn't fit</h3>
      <p class="prose" set:html={`<b>Settling a FORA sale through TollBit.</b> TollBit's API bills the calling account at TollBit's own rates, even for usage the buyer reports itself. It has no call that bills a price another Exchange set (${a(T.content, 'Content')}).`} />
    </Fragment>
    <Figure
      slot="aside"
      src={`${IMG}/tollbit-4.png`}
      title="Both on one site: the order of your CDN rules."
      caption="For your engineers."
      alt="Your CDN asks four questions in order: a request for your FORA file or with a FORA signed link skips TollBit's rule, and FORA's edge checks the link before your origin serves it; TollBit's fetcher goes to your origin; another AI bot gets FORA's refusal or TollBit's paywall, path by path; and readers go to your origin."
    />
  </Band>

